comments.body:
@participant4 I got the file, but very unfortunately that file does not trigger the problem on my system with jellyfin docker.

This seems to be more environment-related than I originally thought. Anyone having this issue mind sharing which installation method is in use and be more specific about the environment jellyfin is running on?

For example, be more specific about the OS, the exact docker image tag if using docker, and the CPU model.

@participant7 Your case makes more sense to me but I still hard to find a sample that would stack the memory more than then probe size much (~1GB).

The sample from @participant4 however is not even a dolby vision file which makes this a more interesting that lead me to believe you are having totally different issues and trying to mix into one.

If you could, can you please provide a (dolby vision) sample file for me to take a look?
